<statement>
<p>
Solve the following linear system.  If the system has an infinite number of solutions, parameterize the solution set in terms of the free variables of the original system.</p>
<p>
<m>\displaystyle{\left\lbrace\begin{array}{ccccccccccc} -{3}{x}\amp-\amp{y}\amp+\amp{5}{z}\amp+\amp{20}{w}\amp+\amp{6}{v}\amp=\amp-{18}\\-{3}{x}\amp-\amp{3}{y}\amp-\amp{2}{z}\amp-\amp{31}{w}\amp-\amp{11}{v}\amp=\amp{35}\\{4}{x}\amp-\amp{6}{y}\amp+\amp{3}{z}\amp-\amp{37}{w}\amp-\amp{35}{v}\amp=\amp-{29}\end{array}\right.}</m></p>
<p>
x = <fillin characters="20"/>  
</p>
<p>
y = <fillin characters="20"/>  
</p>
<p>
z = <fillin characters="20"/>  
</p>
<p>
w = <fillin characters="20"/>  
</p>
<p>
v = <fillin characters="20"/>  

</p>
</statement>
<answer>
<p><ul><li><m>\displaystyle-{5}+{1}{w}+{2}{v}</m></li><li><m>\displaystyle-{2}-{8}{w}-{5}{v}</m></li><li><m>\displaystyle-{7}-{5}{w}-{1}{v}</m></li><li><m>\displaystyle{w}</m></li><li><m>\displaystyle{v}</m></li></ul></p>
</answer>

